          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Darcy Graham Ruled Out As Scotland Confirms Men’s Autumn Test Absence",
          "body": "Scotland have suffered a major setback with record try-scorer Darcy Graham ruled out of the upcoming autumn Tests following a ruptured bicep. The 29-year-old winger sustained the injury during a recent friendly match and is expected to be sidelined for at least 12 weeks. Edinburgh head coach Sean Everitt confirmed the news, stating, “That’s not good news for us and not good news for him.” Graham will miss home encounters against New Zealand, Australia, and Japan."
