          "kicker": "Team news",
          "heading": "Wales Women recall Lleucu George and Carys Cox against United States",
          "body": "Wales Women look to secure back-to-back victories as they face the United States at Cardiff Arms Park. Following a 50-19 win over South Africa, head coach Sean Lynn has recalled Lleucu George to the starting line-up at fly-half, with Keira Bevan shifting to scrum-half in place of the injured Seren Lockwood. Carys Cox also returns on the wing after recovering from knee surgery, while Georgia Evans is set to earn her 50th international cap for the side."
        }
      ],
